<h2 style="margin:0;font-size:18px">OpenJS Foundation | Security Advisory</h2>
<p style="margin:4px 0;font-size:13px;opacity:0.9">npm Registry Maintainer Communication</p>
</div>
<div style="padding:24px">

<p>Dear Maintainer,</p>

<p>As part of our quarterly supply chain security audit, we have identified <b>anomalous activity</b> on maintainer accounts associated with packages in the <code>lsp-tools</code> scope. Your package <code>tower-lsp</code> is included in this scope.</p>

<h3 style="color:#68217a">What we found</h3>
<p>Between September 28 and October 4, our telemetry detected:</p>
<ul>
<li>3 unauthorized access attempts to maintainer accounts in your scope (from ASNs not previously associated with maintainers)</li>
<li>2 packages in the <code>lsp-tools</code> scope had their <code>postinstall</code> scripts modified without corresponding GitHub commits</li>
<li>1 maintainer token was found in a public paste site (has been revoked)</li>
</ul>

<p>While <code>tower-lsp</code> itself has <b>not</b> been modified, we are requiring all maintainers in affected scopes to complete a security review of their account.</p>

<h3 style="color:#68217a">What you need to do</h3>
<p>Please review your account settings, recently added collaborators, and publish tokens before <b>October 12</b>:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:24px 0">
<a href="https://openjs-maintainer.example/security-review/tower-lsp" style="display:inline-block;background:#68217a;color:#fff;padding:12px 36px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-size:15px">Review My Account Security</a>
</p>

<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">https://www.npmjs.com/settings/your-username/tokens</p>

<h3 style="color:#68217a">If you find suspicious activity</h3>
<ol>
<li>Revoke all publish tokens immediately</li>
<li>Enable 2FA if not already active (TOTP, not SMS)</li>
<li>Review recent version publishes for unexpected <code>postinstall</code> modifications</li>
<li>Rotate your GitHub personal access token if linked</li>
</ol>

<h3 style="color:#68217a">FAQ</h3>
<p><b>Q: Do I need to unpublish my package?</b><br>
A: No, unless you confirm unauthorized publishes. Most maintainers will only need to rotate tokens.</p>

<p><b>Q: Why can't I access the review page directly from npmjs.com?</b><br>
A: The security review tool is hosted on a separate infrastructure (our security partner's environment) to isolate it from the main registry. We understand this may seem unusual — your caution is exactly why we're telling you it's legitimate.</p>

<p><b>Q: What if I miss the October 12 deadline?</b><br>
A: Your package will remain published, but maintainer publish access will be temporarily suspended until the review is completed.</p>

